                <pb facs="0392" n="284" sameAs="frus:frus1927v02/pg284"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.11/562: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-04-08T13:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 8, 1927—1
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received April 8—8:55
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>381. Following from American consul at Hankow: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“April 7, 5 p.m. Forty-four Americans left on <hi rendition="#italic">J.
                                Wo</hi> last night and twelve on <hi rendition="#italic">Po
                                Yang;</hi> there now remain seventy-six men, six women and five
                            children. Additional contingents leaving in a day or two.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
